Audit complete. Report written to `scratch_perf/ox/REPORT_batchwide_audit.md`, with the CPU-only probe script alongside it (`scratch_perf/ox/probe_batchwide_audit.py`). Nothing rendered; no tracked file touched (the three `M` entries in `git status` are the other session's in-flight work, not mine).

Findings in brief:

- **Q1 CONFIRMED (b)** — `_compute_samples_per_segment` picks one chord count per segment from the max hull error over **all frames of the batch** (`primitives.py:3018-3021`, kernel atomic-max over frames `logical_pn_taichi.py:405`). Probe: 128 chords over a 19-frame window vs 16–64 per 3-frame window; monotone finer only.
- **Q2 REFUTED** — PN edge/patch levels are per-frame `[T,P,3]`; the `max_diced_triangles` budget's `.sum(1)` sums over **patches**, giving per-frame totals, deliberately frame-local so it can't pop at batch boundaries (`primitives.py:1308-1320, 1794, 1977`).
- **Q3 CONFIRMED (b)** — `_split_promotable`'s `.all(0)` asks corner-uniformity in *every frame of the window* (`scene_builder.py:566-576`): probe shows promotion at T=3, none at T≥6. Values match across paths but arithmetic isn't bit-identical (texel fetch vs barycentric interpolation) and promoted triangles reorder → tie landing shifts. `_dedup_time` fires window-dependently but is value-preserving; `_unify_time` is inert.
- **Q4 CONFIRMED** — STBVH segmentation pads to powers of two and emits dyadic instances of the batch; refit topology builds SAH on batch-union boxes. Pixel effects route through named sites: depth-tie bins broken by merged column index (`raytrace_kernels_taichi.py:976-991, 1140`), ±EPS traversal windows vs f16 boxes, and shadow-march seam de-dup (`:2940-2945`, `wavefront_kernels_taichi.py:2624`).
- **Q5 CONFIRMED (b, conditional)** — `surface_weld_flags`/`surface_closed_axes` reduce `.all()` including time (`surface.py:361-367, 394-399`), so weld topology (triangle count!) and texture wrap-padding are window decisions for grids whose closure varies.
- **Q6** — full sweep table classifies every hit; also flagged the OOM-retry window shrink as an intra-render pop source for all (b) items.
OX EXIT 0
